# .alloc-sink-allowlist (T-2527) — confirmed-safe allocation-sink sites.
#
# check-alloc-sink-clamps.sh flags every with_capacity/Semaphore::new/vec![_;n]/.repeat
# whose size arg is a bare ident or p.<field> and is not inline-clamped or
# binding-clamped. This file acknowledges the sites a human/agent has CONFIRMED are
# bounded-by-construction (upstream guard, internal-derived count, constructor param),
# so the check trends toward empty. One drift-stable signature per line:
#     <relpath>::<sink>(<normalized-arg>)     ( `as usize`/`as u64` casts stripped )
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. Adding a site here is a CLAIM
# that it is safe — cite the reason in the trailing comment so the next reviewer can
# re-verify. When in doubt, clamp the code instead of allowlisting.
#
# --- MCP dispatch handler (crates/termlink-mcp/src/tools.rs) ---
# `count` = p.count, guarded by validate_dispatch_count(p.count) early-return
# (T-2526, MAX_DISPATCH_COUNT=256) BEFORE reaching these two sinks. Bounded.
crates/termlink-mcp/src/tools.rs::with_capacity(count)
crates/termlink-mcp/src/tools.rs::vec!(count)
# `total_tools` is the internally-derived registered-tool count (~215, from the
# registry walk), never caller-supplied. Bounded by the binary's own tool set.
crates/termlink-mcp/src/tools.rs::with_capacity(total_tools)
#
# --- data-plane frame codec (crates/termlink-session/src/codec.rs) ---
# `payload_len` = header.payload_length as usize, where FrameHeader::decode()
# (crates/termlink-protocol/src/data.rs:102) rejects payload_length > MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE
# (16 MiB) one line above via `FrameHeader::decode(&self.header_buf)?`. The bound is
# at the decode boundary, not a `let`-clamp, so the binding-grep can't see it — but
# it is enforced. Confirmed bounded (T-2527 review).
crates/termlink-session/src/codec.rs::vec!(payload_len)
#
# --- event ring buffer constructor (crates/termlink-session/src/events.rs) ---
# `capacity` is the `EventBus::with_capacity(capacity: usize)` constructor param;
# all callers pass the compile-time DEFAULT_CAPACITY constant. Library-API param,
# bounding is the (internal, constant) caller's responsibility. Not caller-supplied.
crates/termlink-session/src/events.rs::with_capacity(capacity)
